## f-string slice 3 — landed on `py-fstrings` in three commits

### Tier split as landed
- **Tier 1 — the lowering (`a3a29a3e`)**: each `{expr}` re-parses as its own snippet packet, nodes merged into the program's packet at offset ids, the snippet's module scope a lambda bridging to the enclosing scope — so interpolations are full expressions of their scope (calls, subscripts, arithmetic, nested quotes). Conversions `!r`/`!s`/`!a` (`py/str-conv`, `py/ascii-conv`), doubled braces, raw `rf`, implicit concatenation with plain strings.
- **Tier 2 — the format-spec mini-language (`b7152eac`)**: `py/format` → `py/format-spec` → str/int/bool/float arms; `py/format-spec` answers a raw string every way out, `py/format` wraps it into the py-str map.

### Format-spec coverage boundary
**Supported**: str fill/align/width/precision/`'s'`; int+bool sign/`#`-with-`d` (CPython-legal no-op)/`0`/width/`,`-and-`_`-grouping/`d b o x X`/`c` (zero-pads via the number path); float fill/align/sign/`0`/width; multi-digit widths; the `0` flag setting fill `'0'` + align `'='` only where the spec gives neither and only before the width starts (`06d`, `<06`, `=6`, `10`, `010`, `05c`, `#05x` all CPython-verified).
**Still refused**: lowering-time `unsupported!` for nested format specs, `=` debug suffix, nested f-strings, multi-line interpolations, bytes; `syntax!` for malformed braces (expecting `}`, single `}`, empty expr, unmatched bracket, unterminated/backslash/comment/conversion-char shapes); runtime ValueError with CPython's own messages for float type codes/precision/grouping, `'n'`/`'z'`/unknown codes, precision on int, `#`/`,` misuse; **TypeError** (CPython's class) for specs on types without `__format__`.

